# Adding a New ECS System

## Step 1 — Ask First
- What entities/components does it operate on?
- Tick interval? (default 50ms)
- Where in system order? (check data dependencies)
- Needs RPC exposure or Lua API?

## Step 2 — Search
Read all files in `include/game/systems/` — check if functionality belongs in an existing system.

## Step 3 — Header
`include/game/systems/<name>.hpp`:
```cpp
#pragma once
#include <game/system.hpp>

class <Name>System : public System {
public:
  <Name>System() : System(50, "<Name>") {}
  void fixedUpdate() override;
};
```

## Step 4 — Implementation
`src/game/systems/<name>.cpp`:
```cpp
void <Name>System::fixedUpdate() {
  auto& state = entt::locator<State>::value();
  auto& registry = state.registry;
  for (auto e : registry.view<RelevantComponent>()) { /* ... */ }
}
```

## Step 5 — Register
Add in `src/game/game_manager.cpp` → `GameManager::start()`:
```cpp
systems.push_back(std::make_shared<<Name>System>());
```
Current order: Tweening → Power → Thermal → Environment → Wireless → CodeExecution → Items

## Step 6 — Verify
Write E2E test in `tests/e2e/`. Run `just test-e2e`.
